# [Here There Be Monsters](htbm)
= Every voice in the mission, in the order the patrol hears them.

The mission's narrative is a chain of incoming hails: TSN Command briefs you, three ships
call for help and are gone by the time you arrive, and their recovered logs tell you what
took them. Each is a scene here, and `story.mast` names one when the beat arrives.

`Audio:` is the recorded line that plays with the message. `Subject:` is the ship the
crew sees if they put the hail on the main screen - the wreck that is calling.

## [Cast](cast)
= Who speaks. Declared so a scene's `Speaker:` resolves to something, and so the voices
= of this mission are readable in one place rather than inferred from story.mast.

### [TSN Command](tsn_command)
Fleet command, a long way off and out of sensor range for most of the patrol.

### [Ensign Rachel](ensign_rachel)
The Artemis's own science officer. Most of the mission's reports are hers.

### [Medical Bay](medical_bay)
The Artemis's sick bay, reporting on the survivor pulled from the escape pod.

### [Whale Watcher 1](whale_watcher)
An Arvonian luxury liner. The first ship to call, and already boarded when it does.

### [TSN Dauntless](dauntless)
A Terran bulk cargo hauler. Its log is the first account of what drains a ship.

### [Odessa](odessa)
A Terran science vessel that came here deliberately, to study the creatures.

### [Unknown Vessel](wolf_spider)
The thing that has been taking the ships. It answers a distress call once.

### [Trapped Miners](hostages)
Held for ransom, and put to work in the mines if nobody pays.

## [Messages](messages)

### [Mission Briefing](mission_briefing)
---
Speaker: tsn_command
Title: Mission Briefing
Audio: audio/SD01C0070
Presentation: portrait
---
This is the "Skulls Refuge Nebula" and looks like you've drawn the short straw for tonights patrol. You are on the outskirts of Terran space, and the twin black holes cause havoc with our long range sensors so we don't know much about this sector.  Several ships traversing this sector have gone missing the last few months. Be on alert and find out whats happen to our ships.

- [Play Message]()

### [Whale Watcher Distress](whale_watcher_distress)
= The first one. A liner, already boarded.
---
Speaker: whale_watcher
Title: Distress Signal
Audio: audio/SD01C0139
Presentation: portrait
---
This is the Arvonian luxury liner "Whale Watcher 1".  We are under attack from an Unknown vessel... Engines...Boarding... Please Help!.....

- [Accept Message]()

